      <slug></slug>
      <title>openSUSE Community</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>openSUSE</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A talk from an openSUSE Community member on Community history, ongoings, problems, challenges, and plans for the future.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;openSUSE, since SUSE Linux 10.0, is open up to the public with beta-testing; development and the release process is no longer all in-house. This talk will cover some thoughts on the response of such a change, other problems and challenges that the community is facing, as well as exciting projects made by the community.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1721">Francis Giannaros</person>
      </persons>
